INT. CAR (MOVING) - NIGHT

SUPER: "2:04 AM"

Wet streetlights slide across the windshield. MO, 30s, rideshare driver, hands at ten and two. In the back, THE WOMAN, 40s, scrubs under a grey coat, a cooler bag on her lap, thumb hovering over her phone.

CLOSE ON the cooler bag. A biohazard sticker. A digital display on it blinking: 03:12.

MO
Hospital's six minutes out. You said the drop's at the transplant door?

THE WOMAN
Side entrance. Don't stop at the main.

Her phone BUZZES. She answers on speaker.

DR. NAIR (V.O.)
Where are you? The patient is on the table and the clock's running.

THE WOMAN
Six minutes. Maybe five.

DR. NAIR (V.O.)
Jen, the courier crashed. I'm told you're riding with a stranger.

JEN
(low, to herself)
Here we go.

ANGLE ON Mo's eyes in the rear-view mirror. A red light ahead. He slows, then runs it.

MO
Sorry. Hold on.

INSERT - THE COOLER DISPLAY

03:09. 03:08.

WE SEE headlights swing in behind them, high beams, closing fast.

JEN
Mo, who is that?

MO
(flooring it)
Not my brother-in-law. Seatbelt.

BACK TO SCENE

DR. NAIR (V.O.)
Jen? Jen, talk to me.

JEN
(gripping the door handle)
Keep the line open. We're not stopping.
